From: dArkOS RG52 Mini port
Subject: The screens swap on Select+R1, not on L3, and the game does not see the pair

The core swapped the top and bottom screens when L3 was pressed (Toggle, by
default: each press). On the RG52 Mini L3 is the switch under the left stick
(BTN_THUMBL, a GPIO key), which a hard push of the stick closes by accident:
the screens changed places in the middle of a game, and the small bottom
screen filled the panel. They now swap when Select and R1 are both down, once
per press of the pair; the "Screen Swap Mode" option (toggle or hold the
button) is gone. Which screen is the prominent one is still chosen in the
core options (Prominent 3DS Screen). L3 is still the 3DS's HOME button.

The game does not see the pair (Super Mario 3D Land paused on its Select):
Select is held back while it is down, up to 30 frames (500 ms), waiting for
R1: released before that it reaches the game then, for 6 frames, held longer
it reaches the game from then on; with R1 already down Select
never reaches it; while the pair is down, until both are up, neither does.

